{"name":"Folk Tales","hex":"#a5c1b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"folk tales","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of folk tale"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/folk_tales"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oral literature","blocks":[{"text":"Oral literature, orature, or folk literature is a genre of literature that is spoken or sung in contrast to that which is written, though much oral literature has been transcribed. There is no standard definition, as anthropologists have used varying descriptions for oral literature or folk literature. A broad conceptualization refers to it as literature characterized by oral transmission and the absence of any fixed form. It includes the stories, legends, and history passed through generations in a spoken form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Kyrgyz_Manaschi%2C_Karakol.jpg/330px-Kyrgyz_Manaschi%2C_Karakol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oral_literature","wikidata":"Q986539"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABooks_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Danish fairy and folk tales 075","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Danish_fairy_and_folk_tales_075.jpg/500px-Danish_fairy_and_folk_tales_075.jpg","ratio":0.6197053406998159,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danish_fairy_and_folk_tales_075.jpg","